# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# id: fuzz.osc52-invalid-base64-swallowed
# geometry: 20 2
# expect-line: 0 = ok
# expect-cursor: 0 2
#
# An OSC 52 clipboard set carrying a payload that is not valid base64. The
# sequence must be consumed without writing the grid, without a host reply,
# and without desynchronizing the parser — the printable bytes that follow
# land exactly where a clean parse puts them. Minimized shape of the FZ2
# invalid-payload inputs; the fuzzer explores, the corpus keeps the point.
#
# Escapes: \e ESC, \r CR, \n LF, \t HT, \\ backslash, \xNN one byte.
# Every other character is emitted literally. Lines add no implicit newline.

\e]52;c;%%%not-base64%%%\x07ok
